[{:db/id "q-10978/selection/66677756267c585947ba18d3cd4adbe97174e07b89b659668789a799f3380105" :answer/id #uuid "fb09bab5-1f31-56c1-8aaf-5580ef2ace97" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{19}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10978/selection/53a62adc469f7106cfcc253972af70d0b351ee4c505c92859749c553ee85bd38" :answer/id #uuid "6e53459d-c26f-581f-b92e-5cfdc3e630c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{11}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10978/selection/4bf6dd19b67f21e3d989056b85307162fae5b4b119455833dfa737e1150d56ad" :answer/id #uuid "88921aa9-5ce7-5e3e-aa94-34c52a208bc4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{27}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10978/selection/99e2b5754349f37ea380857308f6291cb13b27c6d7da23f5f1905ba4bf86e8c5" :answer/id #uuid "202ffa58-272b-5ce4-9590-e7cb3244049f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{19}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10978/selection/b2b2487c52633be6396d294ebadec1265f7827ec4e8b5458042006050873a19a" :answer/id #uuid "6d8539f1-4620-5fe3-bbb0-2ccce10dc720" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{17}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10978/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "bac6f17e-69ff-50d1-82e1-0fbc84fa2799" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-10978/selection/53a62adc469f7106cfcc253972af70d0b351ee4c505c92859749c553ee85bd38" :answer-field/choices ["q-10978/selection/66677756267c585947ba18d3cd4adbe97174e07b89b659668789a799f3380105" "q-10978/selection/53a62adc469f7106cfcc253972af70d0b351ee4c505c92859749c553ee85bd38" "q-10978/selection/4bf6dd19b67f21e3d989056b85307162fae5b4b119455833dfa737e1150d56ad" "q-10978/selection/99e2b5754349f37ea380857308f6291cb13b27c6d7da23f5f1905ba4bf86e8c5" "q-10978/selection/b2b2487c52633be6396d294ebadec1265f7827ec4e8b5458042006050873a19a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-10978" :question/id #uuid "14aae701-3d97-58e0-b9cc-218ca30f5a80" :question/math-academy-id "q-10978" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/assets/09482b1e9903bff25b16b2239975831e6d54440a8f8ea78f5739b0eafee3d9e8.png)\n\nFind the area between the curve $y=-2{x}^{2}-x+3$, the $x$-axis and the $y$-axis, shown above." :question/worked-solution "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(-2{x}^{2}-x+3)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-1{\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\,\\text{d}x+3{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2\\cdot {\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}|}_{0}^{1}-1\\cdot {\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}|}_{0}^{1}+3x{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-2(\\frac{1}{3}-0)-1(\\frac{1}{2}-0)+3(1-0) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{1}{2}+3 \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-10978/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96967f25-565a-5338-878e-00fd30055772"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-10978"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-345319/field-1/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" :answer/id #uuid "5e57ad0b-9483-526c-890b-8610e0c25573" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-345319/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "02cd5950-75bb-531f-baa4-a242087bb56b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-345319/field-1/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" :answer-field/choices ["q-345319/field-1/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-345319" :question/id #uuid "af0957a3-156c-55af-b348-c5c2666a8fa7" :question/math-academy-id "q-345319" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/assets/0a4b4be4f7de918b847245372077e159f60f3834bb37ef00f4873e63b4cea894.png)\n\nA region is bounded by the curve $y={e}^{x}$ and the $x$-axis between $x=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)$ and $x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)$, as shown above. Find the area $A$ of the region. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{x}{|}_{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}-{e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)} \\\\  & =2-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-345319/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96967f25-565a-5338-878e-00fd30055772"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-345319"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-345322/field-1/cedce138738816f1e959edfd5049bf0c6bcf0acc69b898c7f84479cb3a782ce3" :answer/id #uuid "dd04ae4e-8b2a-583a-99ac-cefd48c3c441" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-345322/field-1/c43b27454cd69f1b6f4b793e211f4f4f6e40314b87f5b1c35a69172a60fcd818" :answer/id #uuid "f2234af5-c4b4-528e-a73d-9112c3bcf211" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-345322/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "3a308356-6fe7-5b58-823a-c078c0fdfb17" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-345322/field-1/cedce138738816f1e959edfd5049bf0c6bcf0acc69b898c7f84479cb3a782ce3" :answer-field/choices ["q-345322/field-1/cedce138738816f1e959edfd5049bf0c6bcf0acc69b898c7f84479cb3a782ce3" "q-345322/field-1/c43b27454cd69f1b6f4b793e211f4f4f6e40314b87f5b1c35a69172a60fcd818"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-345322" :question/id #uuid "7dc244c3-54c6-5170-b8f9-917b4e9e083b" :question/math-academy-id "q-345322" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/assets/66bf8c1144de1ad65938345d2937fddd6fb43ec4822a2b98a9b5383ca2609567.png)\n\nA region is bounded by the curve $y=-2{x}^{2}+3$ and the $x$-axis between $x=0$ and $x=1$, as shown above. Find the area $A$ of the region. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(-2{x}^{2}+3)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(-2\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+3x){|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(-\\frac{2}{3}+3)-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-345322/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96967f25-565a-5338-878e-00fd30055772"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-345322"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-54474/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer/id #uuid "c381f770-778e-5ccd-993b-3797afeba2a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-54474/selection/d1af04a07c3006a9711c776ada92f7f462fd920b4bd9984795d271d30b151b69" :answer/id #uuid "c057d538-1733-5266-b831-f8d63c0eb129" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\sqrt[3]{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-54474/selection/6b95511de4de11a307ef0b59561676b4ba5acdacebc5c441c2ab3b04050b282b" :answer/id #uuid "d12a0620-00d1-5952-a69e-06e1a9ba761b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-54474/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "d6c226fd-3c8d-58cc-b2e6-6f70d51d8e1a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-54474/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "01063069-e246-5f12-b01d-b72666e18038" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-54474/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "555f6e53-800c-5247-a583-8629aac2480f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-54474/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer-field/choices ["q-54474/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" "q-54474/selection/d1af04a07c3006a9711c776ada92f7f462fd920b4bd9984795d271d30b151b69" "q-54474/selection/6b95511de4de11a307ef0b59561676b4ba5acdacebc5c441c2ab3b04050b282b" "q-54474/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-54474/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-54474" :question/id #uuid "14752328-fec5-5213-a8b6-ccc1fe3ce177" :question/math-academy-id "q-54474" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/assets/de15e1e9433a3560cbc8268904f4f62fbbb721c3b5b9a700c59fea0941829406.png)\n\nThe area of the shaded region between the curve $y={x}^{3}+8$ and the $x$-axis is given by the integral expression below. What is the value of $a?$\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{a}^{2}({x}^{3}+8)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To get $a$, we need to find the $x$-intercepts of the curve $y={x}^{3}+8.$ \n\nWe solve the equation for $y=0$: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}+8 & =y \\\\ {x}^{3}+8 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{3} & =-8 \\\\ x & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=-2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-54474/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96967f25-565a-5338-878e-00fd30055772"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-54474"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-316022/field-1/1f6fb6227fc77ae549aa4157c376626013e8a2df91c2ab3109c2e75c1420c78f" :answer/id #uuid "7ad04aee-4354-5499-a9c4-5d32782153cd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt{3}+\\ln(2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316022/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "cfbc56d0-6cf5-56e8-832a-e1f5ce426489" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-316022/field-1/1f6fb6227fc77ae549aa4157c376626013e8a2df91c2ab3109c2e75c1420c78f" :answer-field/choices ["q-316022/field-1/1f6fb6227fc77ae549aa4157c376626013e8a2df91c2ab3109c2e75c1420c78f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-316022" :question/id #uuid "3dc8a6c1-7592-5eeb-a313-53d3c7edaf54" :question/math-academy-id "q-316022" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/assets/b5432ed129d85a3718f8e5ebe0cca141731c366d1b32e8e72d0916c60c34de2c.png)\n\nA region in the $x$-$y$ plane is bounded by the curve $y={sec}^{2}⁡x+\\frac{1}{x}$, and the $x$-axis between $x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ and $x=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$, as shown above. \nFind the area $A$ of the region. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}({sec}^{2}⁡(x)+\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}{sec}^{2}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,+\\,{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)){|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{3}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{3})-(\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{\\pi /3}{\\pi /6} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-316022/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96967f25-565a-5338-878e-00fd30055772"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-316022"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-73333/selection/e0bd991ac2e2f2a23ec920e03c6d5103be6b20c12a25d724ab290d4ba5292c3e" :answer/id #uuid "9a75289d-0f98-54fe-aaf7-8b1c9899a80f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73333/selection/adbad78d33491a071139fe589fefda7e9ba65cf97ebbcae14d252ac90459e198" :answer/id #uuid "317e331e-877c-5961-8298-0690cd98a699" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73333/selection/7b1b8538b264eef6681d0ab5f3b14d51b6cdff67f34fba59d0886ae5c6acf80a" :answer/id #uuid "ee8ada9f-2cfa-5d32-80d7-fcb52fe23c08" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73333/selection/82f0679237d603c9b88d77fbc6f240065a24a3716631fab4d9f58426a7f011e5" :answer/id #uuid "cb61c6c0-438a-53fc-8c13-638c6b8a9846" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73333/selection/35d0af53e25a7911f6d08c6d063fcf9231a1273a16a0f7056530d6f5d5dfbdd8" :answer/id #uuid "1f112e36-2d53-59a1-b16a-8f9b49ca15e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\pi }{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73333/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1c15c80e-3510-55b8-9353-1985f3adce45" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-73333/selection/adbad78d33491a071139fe589fefda7e9ba65cf97ebbcae14d252ac90459e198" :answer-field/choices ["q-73333/selection/e0bd991ac2e2f2a23ec920e03c6d5103be6b20c12a25d724ab290d4ba5292c3e" "q-73333/selection/adbad78d33491a071139fe589fefda7e9ba65cf97ebbcae14d252ac90459e198" "q-73333/selection/7b1b8538b264eef6681d0ab5f3b14d51b6cdff67f34fba59d0886ae5c6acf80a" "q-73333/selection/82f0679237d603c9b88d77fbc6f240065a24a3716631fab4d9f58426a7f011e5" "q-73333/selection/35d0af53e25a7911f6d08c6d063fcf9231a1273a16a0f7056530d6f5d5dfbdd8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-73333" :question/id #uuid "61cc7b90-6261-5d84-a76c-eb58b2277a06" :question/math-academy-id "q-73333" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/assets/1819bad0219f1709a01100daad00beb25a8bbc3688f9fe7c41be53bad8010455.png)\n\nA region is bounded by the curve $y=-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}$, the $x$-axis, and the lines $x=-0.5$ and $x=0.5$, as shown above. What is the area of the region?" :question/worked-solution "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-0.5}^{0.5}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{-0.5}^{0.5}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x{|}_{-0.5}^{0.5} \\\\  & =-(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(0.5)-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-0.5)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+(-\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is $\\frac{\\pi }{3}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-73333/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6ad216da-1bcf-5b87-9436-918ef1e5015a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73333"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-103824/selection/986e06f062dcc0ad37fbb185f7e0d56b0fd8e74b571035e7dc0af3d06af89951" :answer/id #uuid "6c04dcf5-bb0e-519d-bea6-29b3eaafd011" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103824/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "8a2f18ac-79ee-5da0-af4b-3b111f5d3115" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103824/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "02d2d42c-a2f6-5794-98d1-e9f45e363f20" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103824/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "8aaa62df-b3d3-5788-932b-ac74df33f711" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103824/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "edb5b488-bf49-5b1d-877c-a110c0b28fc5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103824/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8d637e68-da4f-5b6c-a95a-d87f9ad2692b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-103824/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-103824/selection/986e06f062dcc0ad37fbb185f7e0d56b0fd8e74b571035e7dc0af3d06af89951" "q-103824/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-103824/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-103824/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-103824/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-103824" :question/id #uuid "0c21d4e0-baa2-59e6-b265-1bfdd4a8ba84" :question/math-academy-id "q-103824" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/assets/97cf633bce7a8eeef443757e62d52f356c911b6aee3d8019d434d514416b0049.png)\n\nA region is bounded by the curve $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and the $x$-axis between $x=-\\pi $ and $x=0$, as shown above. What is the area of the region?" :question/worked-solution "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{0}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x{|}_{-\\pi }^{0} \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)-(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\pi )) \\\\  & =-1-(1) \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is $2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-103824/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6ad216da-1bcf-5b87-9436-918ef1e5015a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-103824"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-345381/field-1/ccc5b7f3cfdb4c2dfc0e1f31be54559a1ab3adaf142e500fc1f1b7bc87e93b08" :answer/id #uuid "6747e758-6554-57f1-a112-5e4fcdd611c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-345381/field-1/438469ab2d71e1bb8b63f3164bacb1bbb54e29062b14dce6a666b63ac0081609" :answer/id #uuid "aa3dc2fa-4986-554c-83a6-9a6de5d5401f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-345381/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "55f5b3e8-bdcb-5dee-90c0-d3879f2619f3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-345381/field-1/ccc5b7f3cfdb4c2dfc0e1f31be54559a1ab3adaf142e500fc1f1b7bc87e93b08" :answer-field/choices ["q-345381/field-1/ccc5b7f3cfdb4c2dfc0e1f31be54559a1ab3adaf142e500fc1f1b7bc87e93b08" "q-345381/field-1/438469ab2d71e1bb8b63f3164bacb1bbb54e29062b14dce6a666b63ac0081609"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-345381" :question/id #uuid "79d1f903-1ab4-5a5d-94d4-eace512d810a" :question/math-academy-id "q-345381" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/assets/dce89dbea62566c0ee897bffe0638458970799bafdc7d7c8e5084328fef38bef.png)\n\nA region is bounded by the curve $y=-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}$, the $x$-axis, and the lines $x=-1$ and $x=1$, as shown above. Find the area $A$ of the region. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-arcsin\\,(\\frac{x}{2}){|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =-(arcsin\\,(\\frac{1}{2})-arcsin\\,(-\\frac{1}{2})) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+(-\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is \n\n$$\nA=-{\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{\\pi }{3}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-345381/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6ad216da-1bcf-5b87-9436-918ef1e5015a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-345381"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-345343/field-1/80f9bea33aa6a89d127ee9002c35787893c3c59b57df469ba089cea1a4a6a472" :answer/id #uuid "0e1f9a6a-e10b-58a2-a01b-182ae2eeed8f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-345343/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "8715be83-ce41-55ca-9341-52a474fd23f8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-345343/field-1/80f9bea33aa6a89d127ee9002c35787893c3c59b57df469ba089cea1a4a6a472" :answer-field/choices ["q-345343/field-1/80f9bea33aa6a89d127ee9002c35787893c3c59b57df469ba089cea1a4a6a472"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-345343" :question/id #uuid "10fa10cd-fc6f-507a-99f5-6fa17f1da5d9" :question/math-academy-id "q-345343" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/assets/34eb73b6bd93f9a45b666ed0599719a09b54948d1d81b14ceea9b46f99b75054.png)\n\nFind the area between the curve $y=-{x}^{2}-1$, the $x$-axis, and the line $x=-1$ and $x=1$ (shown above). Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}(-{x}^{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}|}_{-1}^{1}-x{|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =-(\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{(-1)^{3}}{3})-(1-(-1)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}-2 \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is \n\n$$\nA=-{\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{8}{3}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-345343/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6ad216da-1bcf-5b87-9436-918ef1e5015a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-345343"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-316024/field-1/e7e505d325c3cadeeeaf26a0afda20aaa10bea508f9739931632d1057683cd77" :answer/id #uuid "f8087994-f633-5222-bc42-b0ed8f245d96" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316024/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "711f7b04-3786-56a4-83fc-600b47fb0b3d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-316024/field-1/e7e505d325c3cadeeeaf26a0afda20aaa10bea508f9739931632d1057683cd77" :answer-field/choices ["q-316024/field-1/e7e505d325c3cadeeeaf26a0afda20aaa10bea508f9739931632d1057683cd77"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-316024" :question/id #uuid "0898c71c-a5cb-5f15-ba0d-a57bf7aea007" :question/math-academy-id "q-316024" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/assets/d282e4afd0a66dd79fecf474da9f618a5970197943044d24208f86c4c43781e6.png)\n\nA region is bounded by the curve $y=-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}$, the $x$-axis, and the lines $x=-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ and $x=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$, as shown above. Find the area $A$ of the region. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-\\sqrt{2}/2}^{\\sqrt{2}/2}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{2}/2}^{\\sqrt{2}/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x{|}_{-\\sqrt{2}/2}^{\\sqrt{2}/2} \\\\  & =-(arcsin\\,(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})-arcsin\\,(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{4}+(-\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is \n\n$$\nA=-{\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-316024/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6ad216da-1bcf-5b87-9436-918ef1e5015a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-316024"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-781"] :question/problem "Find the area between the curve $y=x^2-2x+2,$ the $x$-axis, and the lines $x=0$ and $x=2.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/assets/6b85f10cde49017eac1c56ad1b8abbcdf3033a367d5e1eb162dd89fbb6141461.png)" :question/worked-solution "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}({x}^{2}-2x+2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-2{\\int }_{0}^{2}x\\,\\text{d}x+2{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}|}_{0}^{2}-2\\cdot {\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}|}_{0}^{2}+2x{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{8}{3}-0)-2(2-0)+2(2-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}-4+4 \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-782"] :question/worked-solution "First, we find the intersections of the curve with the $x$-axis:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-1 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =1 \\\\ x & =\\pm 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe draw a sketch of the region, as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/assets/9b78aad41f84f6a6997914bd8d4243f30cb0ebea4edb5305962dc11c7a46a807.png)\n\nWe want the area between the curve $y=x^2-1$ and the $x$-axis, from $x=-1$ to $x=1.$ To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}({x}^{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}|}_{-1}^{1}-x{|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{3}-(-\\frac{1}{3}))-(1-(-1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}-2 \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is $\\dfrac{4}{3}.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
